From c171caf3aefb3bded5fdbd7acdbc67332cf79833 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: CipherScope <dev@cipherscope.io>
Date: Wed, 23 Sep 2026 06:39:35 -0600
Subject: [PATCH 36/48] crypto: vendor mldsa-native v2.0.0 for ML-DSA-44
 signature verification

Ark-0's M1 adds an experimental tapscript opcode inside P2MR leaves that
verifies an ML-DSA-44 (FIPS 204) signature. This is the verifier it will
use, on its own, before any consensus code: mldsa-native v2.0.0 (commit
834a90d5e846ffa1e1611bd24e160bb2e9b86d35, Apache-2.0 OR ISC OR MIT),
taken unmodified from the release tarball into src/crypto/mldsa44/.

- Only the portable C code is taken and built, as the single translation
  unit mldsa_native.c. The assembly backends are left out, so consensus
  does not depend on which implementation a machine selects; the AVX2
  verifiers of the pq-crystals reference and of PQClean accepted some
  invalid signatures until mid-2026.
- bitcoin_mldsa44_config.h selects ML-DSA-44, the bitcoin_mldsa symbol
  prefix and a verification-only build: nodes never create keys or
  signatures, so key generation and signing are compiled out, and with
  them the need for a randombytes() implementation.
- src/crypto/mldsa44.h exposes one function, MLDSA44Verify: ML-DSA.Verify
  of FIPS 204, the external interface of pure ML-DSA with a context
  string. It is not the external-mu interface and not HashML-DSA.

src/crypto/mldsa44/README.md records where every file came from.
