new file mode 100644
index 0000000..44844f9
--- /dev/null
+++ b/src/crypto/mldsa44/README.md
@@ -0,0 +1,27 @@
+# ML-DSA-44 verification (vendored mldsa-native)
+
+This directory is [mldsa-native](https://github.com/pq-code-package/mldsa-native)
+v2.0.0, commit `834a90d5e846ffa1e1611bd24e160bb2e9b86d35`, taken from the release tarball
+`https://github.com/pq-code-package/mldsa-native/archive/refs/tags/v2.0.0.tar.gz`
+(SHA-256 `97a7305c32b62cbcae97891823176e18ca96d9eaafc3728587d75bb113862a40`). mldsa-native implements FIPS 204 (ML-DSA) and is
+licensed Apache-2.0 OR ISC OR MIT; see `LICENSE`.
+
+What was taken, unmodified: `LICENSE`, `mldsa/mldsa_native.c`,
+`mldsa/mldsa_native.h`, `mldsa/mldsa_native_config.h`, and the `.c`, `.h` and
+`.inc` files of `mldsa/src/` and `mldsa/src/fips202/`.
+
+What was left out: `mldsa/src/native/` and `mldsa/src/fips202/native/`, the
+assembly backends, and everything outside `mldsa/`. Only the portable C code
+is built, on every platform, so that consensus never depends on which
+implementation a machine happens to select. (The AVX2 verifiers of the
+pq-crystals reference and of PQClean each accepted some invalid signatures
+until pq-crystals fixed them on 2026-06-03; PQClean's copy was never fixed.)
+
+What was added: `bitcoin_mldsa44_config.h`, which selects ML-DSA-44, the
+`bitcoin_mldsa` symbol prefix, and a verification-only build; and this file.
+
+The library is compiled as the single translation unit `mldsa_native.c` and is
+used only through `src/crypto/mldsa44.h`. It is checked by
+`src/test/mldsa44_tests.cpp` against the NIST ACVP sigVer vectors for the
+external, pure ML-DSA-44 interface and against the Wycheproof ML-DSA-44
+verification vectors.
